{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 13:32:05","profile":{"player_id":"100376","last_updated":"12/11/2026 13:32","fullname":"Lucy Kay Hamilton","short_display_name":"L Hamilton","name":"Lucy Hamilton","gender":"F","dob":"08/05/2006","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Australia","nationality_id":"1","nationality":"Australia","nationality_short_code":"AUS","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"2","text":"Bowler","role":"Bowler"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"1","text":"Left-arm fast"},"writeup":"<p>Lucy Hamilton is one of the most exciting young prospects in Australian cricket, known for her height, left-arm pace, and ability to swing the ball. A product of the Sunshine Coast Cricket Club, she made headlines as a teenage prodigy, becoming the second-youngest debutant for Queensland in the WNCL era at just 15 years old. By 2026, she has established herself as a key figure in domestic cricket and a future star on the international stage.</p>\r\n<p>Playing for the Brisbane Heat, Hamilton became the youngest player in Women's Big Bash League history to claim a five-wicket haul. At 18 years old, she recorded remarkable figures of 5/8 against the Melbourne Stars, dismissing top-tier batters including Meg Lanning and Annabel Sutherland.</p>\r\n<p>Her rapid rise led to her first overseas franchise contract, being signed by the Delhi Capitals for the 2026 Women's Premier League (WPL) season.&nbsp;</p>","relation":null,"social_details":{"social_platform":[{"social_platform_id":"1","social_platform_name":"facebook","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"2","social_platform_name":"twitter","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"3","social_platform_name":"instagram","social_platform_url":"https://www.instagram.com/_lucy.hamilton_/?hl=en"},{"social_platform_id":"4","social_platform_name":"youtube","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"5","social_platform_name":"pinterest","social_platform_url":""},{"socia